What:   `shpool rename [OLD_NAME] NEW_NAME`, and a SHPOOL_SESSION_ID that never changes, so that
        remote-gosh can rename the shpool sessions behind its terminals (remote-gosh issue #3).
Where:  the daemon's session table, attach, ttl reaper, prompt injection, the protocol, the CLI,
        and tests (shpool/tests/rename.rs). Session directories become sessions/<id>.
Shape:  adds a command and a protocol message, and reshapes how long-lived parts of the daemon
        find a session (by id, not by name). Protocol version 0.4.4.
Needs:  nothing before it.
Status: offered upstream as https://github.com/shell-pool/shpool/pull/459 (closes shpool #57).
        Drop this patch when a shpool release includes it, and move the pin to that release.

